From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 8 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: a library call on a bound opponent that is gone gives
 the empty value of its type, not "no value", at n > 2

Owner rule OQ3: a dead bound opponent means no effect on that opponent, never a Lua error. When the Lua value 1 is bound to a
seat that is eliminated (or no opponent lives), the functions that read or act on that side took their empty exit with
`return 0`, which pushes no Lua value. A script that compares the answer (GetLocationCount(1-tp,LOCATION_MZONE)>0, Diabellstar)
then failed with "attempt to compare nil with number". Now such a function pushes the empty value of its type: 0 for a count, a
zone mask or a zone list (two zeros for GetLocationCount, GetMZoneCount, GetLocationCountFromEx and one per activity for
GetActivityCount), false for a check or an action that did nothing, nil for a flag label, an empty group for a group query.
The new fold::gone_* helpers push only in an active fold scope (n > 2) and only for the Lua values 0 and 1. PLAYER_NONE,
PLAYER_ALL, the values above 1 and every call with two duelists keep the stock result (no value), byte for byte.
---
 fold.h      | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libcard.cpp |  6 ++--
 libduel.cpp | 82 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 3 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fold.h b/fold.h
index 8784f0b..2dfa2ff 100644
--- a/fold.h
+++ b/fold.h
@@ -280,6 +280,44 @@ inline void push_player(lua_State* L, duel* pduel, uint8_t d, bool bind = true)
 	lua_pushinteger(L, pduel->lua->fold_out(d));
 }
 
+// OQ3 (owner rule): a bound opponent that is gone means "no effect on that opponent", never a Lua error.
+// When a library function took its empty result because the side v has no seat any more (the bound opponent was
+// eliminated since the bind, or no opponent lives), it gives the empty VALUE of its type (0, false, nil or an empty
+// group), so that a script that compares the answer ("> 0", "== 0") reads a value and not "nothing".
+// gone_side is true only in a scope (n > 2) and only for the Lua values 0 and 1. PLAYER_NONE, PLAYER_ALL and the kind (d)
+// values keep the stock result (no value). At n == 2, or without a scope, every gone_* helper returns 0 and pushes
+// nothing: the stock result, same bytes. Each helper returns the number of values it pushed (a Lua C function's result).
+inline bool gone_side(duel* pduel, uint8_t v) {
+	return v <= 1 && active(pduel) != nullptr;
+}
+// n times the integer 0 (a count, a zone mask, a zone list)
+inline int gone_int(lua_State* L, duel* pduel, uint8_t v, int n = 1) {
+	if(!gone_side(pduel, v))
+		return 0;
+	luaL_checkstack(L, n, nullptr);
+	for(int i = 0; i < n; ++i)
+		lua_pushinteger(L, 0);
+	return n;
+}
+inline int gone_bool(lua_State* L, duel* pduel, uint8_t v) {
+	if(!gone_side(pduel, v))
+		return 0;
+	lua_pushboolean(L, 0);
+	return 1;
+}
+inline int gone_nil(lua_State* L, duel* pduel, uint8_t v) {
+	if(!gone_side(pduel, v))
+		return 0;
+	lua_pushnil(L);
+	return 1;
+}
+inline int gone_group(lua_State* L, duel* pduel, uint8_t v) {
+	if(!gone_side(pduel, v))
+		return 0;
+	interpreter::pushobject(L, pduel->new_group());
+	return 1;
+}
+
 } // namespace fold
 
 #endif /* FOLD_H_ */
